# Push after pytest

The human allows `git push` to `origin` when convenient, under these conditions:

- Run the pytest tests related to the change first (`pytest -m "not full"` at minimum; the full suite when the change touches solve, benches, or CI). Push only if they pass.
- Never run `git push --force`, rewrite pushed history, or delete remote branches unless the human explicitly asks.
- Each fix is its own commit with its own version bump (see `CONTRIBUTING.md`).
- After pushing, check the GitHub CI run and fix a red job in a new commit.
